[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092845706","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108652#issuecomment-3092845706","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108652","id":3092845706,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64WRSK","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-20T03:18:46Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T03:18:46Z","body":"Option 2 indicates the behavior when dragging a selected key. Then the new key can always be considered selected.\n\nHowever, for clarity, it would be fine to explain that the insertion of new keys and the movement of keys are performed by snapping them to the nearest frame.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092845706/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092892619","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108652#issuecomment-3092892619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108652","id":3092892619,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc64WcvL","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-20T03:23:01Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T03:30:51Z","body":"However, it is important to note that there is no perfect “frame” in Godot animations. Since ticks for playingback and drawing are always processed as double float point numbers, it is dangerous to make misunderstand for users that Godot has complete frames.\n\nIt might be better to use terms such as “frame time” or “virtual frame”, but I'm not quite sure that it is suite in English. @AThousandShips @Mickeon Do you have any ideas?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3092892619/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"